ic level. France won both golds in men’s foil, Italy were Kings of épée whilst, after a close run thing in the team event, Hungary were dominant at sabre."] "\n\n" [:p {} "A major surprise was the win of " [:a {:href "/athletes/20779"} "Irene Camber-Corno"] " over reigning champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/20737"} "Ilona Elek-Schacherer"] " in a barrage to decide the gold medal whilst the failure of the French at épée was also a shock."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Italy with three golds and eight medals in total was the most successful nation and, individually, Italian " [:a {:href "/athletes/22677"} "Edoardo Mangiarotti"] " with two golds and two silvers was the outstanding fencer of the Games.\nAustralia, Japan and the USSR were amongst the nations to appear in Olympic fencing for the first time."] "\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Events"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {} "Status"] "\n" [:th {} "Date"] "\n" [:th {} "Participants"] "\n" [:th {} "NOCs"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/86512"} "Foil, Individual, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "23 – 24 July 1952"] "\n" [:td {} "61"] "\n" [:td {} "25"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/86573"} "Foil, Team, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "21 – 22 July 1952"] "\n" [:td {} "77"] "\n" [:td {} "15"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/86533"} "Épée, Individual, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "27 – 28 July 1952"] "\n" [:td {} "76"] "\n" [:td {} "29"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/86618"} "Épée, Team, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "25 – 26 July 1952"] "\n" [:td {} "97"] "\n" [:td {} "19"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/86553"} "Sabre, Individual, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "31 July –  1 August 1952"] "\n" [:td {} "66"] "\n" [:td {} "26"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/result